index 0b99f893..63521ceb 100644
--- a/docs/overview.md
+++ b/docs/overview.md
@@ -601,6 +601,7 @@ User-facing modules each get one `lym <module>` namespace:
   `PR-Review` lands the task through a GitHub pull request when the resolver says so: it pushes the task branch, opens or finds the pull request, sets its title and body from the change description, records it and waits on it, and otherwise passes.
   The wait takes no parent lock: it gates and pushes the agent's commits through the `pr-review` gate key, never onto a merged pull request, and mails a failure to the agent, reads the pull request at most once a minute and before each gate, and ends Done when the pull request is merged or approved at the gated head, or when the operator's `lym loom pr-continue` makes the row close it, and Stuck on any other ending; a pause that covers the run holds it, and the driver strand's mark reads `PR #<n>`.
   `Finalize` takes the parent lock first, merges the parent into the task in place, resolving a conflict with the conflict session under the lock; it runs the `finalize` gate key and the merge fixer in finalize mode, lands on the parent with the credit block and releases the lock on every exit.
+  It frees the lock while its fixer or fix review works, then takes it again at the front of the queue, merges the parent anew and verifies under the lock before it lands.
   Finalize never reroutes: a fixer change over the caps goes to its fix review, which reads only the fixer's commits, and a rejection hands the findings back to the fixer to fix in place, for up to `finalize_fix_review_rounds` reviews; an approval lands it, and the last review that does not approve halts for the operator, whose `lym loom circling accept` lands the change with the open findings in the change description.
   A halt at `Parent-Align` or `Finalize` (a spent or over-cap fixer, fix reviews out of rounds) is handed back to the orch through every driver, and the status marks it `hand_back`.
   On a loom run, tapestry, darn, pawl or sampler, a fixer's escalate halts with `EscalateStopPrefix` instead, is not marked `hand_back` and goes to the arbiter first, reaching the orch only as the arbiter's hand-on.
